OL,3,GNEWSAThe men who lit a match under an
OL,4,ARAF base - and Welsh nationalism
OL,5,
OL,6,FIn the early hours of 8 September 1936,
OL,7,Fthree middle-aged academics with no
OL,8,Fprior history of criminality trudged
OL,9,Fthrough a field, armed with petrol
OL,10,Fcans, to set fire to an RAF bombing
OL,11,Fschool.
OL,13,FThis was arguably the event that placed
OL,14,FWelsh nationalism on the map, with
OL,15,Freportedly 20% of the population coming
OL,16,Fout in support, one historian said.
OL,18,FPlaid Cymru founders Lewis Valentine,
OL,19,FSaunders Lewis and DJ Williams were
OL,20,Fbitterly opposed to RAF Penrhos being
OL,21,Fon the Llyn Peninsula - the spiritual
OL,22,Froute on the North Wales Pilgrims Way.
OL,23,APub: 07-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
FL,434,430,260,140,0,100
